  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">African Fertilizer Financing Mechanism_African Emergency Food Production Facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The African Union has established the African Fertilizer Financing Mechanism (AFFM) under the African Development Bank (AfDB) through the Abuja Declaration on Fertilizer for the African Green Revolution. As a response to the 2022 food crisis AfDB has applied for funds to AFFM under its African Emergency Food Production Facility (AEFPF). Under the AFFM credit guarantees will be offered to fertilizer suppliers, fertilizer value chains will be strengthened, and extension services provided. The overall objective is to increase availability of fertilizer and usage by smallholder farmers in Kenya, Mozambique and Uganda.</narrative>
  </description>
